{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}How It Works | ISDS Thematic Watcher{% endblock %}
{% block description %}The whole instrument on one chart, drawn deterministically from the repository it describes: the nine public sources, the automated pipeline, the multi-stage AI-assisted classification and review workflow, the operator's verification column, and every Monday deliverable.{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="measure">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="{{ root }}index.html">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">How It Works</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <p class="page-kicker">The instrument</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">How the instrument works</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      The whole system on one chart, drawn directly from the repository it
      describes &mdash; every box and arrow cites the file that implements it.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="measure">
    <div class="doc-body">
      <p>
        Read it top to bottom. The first band is the nine public sources checked
        on every run. Beneath it the work divides into four columns:
        <strong>the machine</strong> &mdash; the automated pipeline that collects,
        de-duplicates, scores, and quality-gates each candidate development;
        <strong>what gets sent</strong> &mdash; the emails and site updates each
        stage produces; <strong>the AI-assisted review workflow</strong> &mdash; a
        multi-stage classification and review process in which separate model
        passes, each running under different instructions and each box naming the
        model it runs on, screen, analyse, challenge, and edit the week&rsquo;s
        output, and in which a verification pass can block publication; and
        <strong>Emory&rsquo;s verification column</strong> &mdash; the checks the
        operator carries out by hand. The moving dots trace work flowing through
        the system. On a desktop browser, hovering over any box shows its full
        description and the exact code behind it.
      </p>
      <p class="caveat">
        <strong>These passes are not independent researchers.</strong> They share
        source material, prompt lineage, model family, and this project&rsquo;s
        framing assumptions, and can therefore share the same errors. Agreement
        between passes is not corroboration.
      </p>
      <p class="caveat">
        <strong>Claims here are machine-assisted and remain provisional</strong>
        unless an item is individually marked human-verified. One operator review
        cycle has been logged &mdash; 2026-07-18 &mdash; covering three claims from
        the research record: one verified against a primary source, one partially
        verified, one not reviewed. No digest entry and no sentence on this website
        has been checked by a human against its original source; every archived
        digest entry to date is machine-screened only. The operator has no access
        to paywalled sources, so claims resting on them cannot be operator-verified
        at all.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figure class="workflow-figure">
    <div class="workflow-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Workflow chart; scrolls horizontally on small screens" tabindex="0">
      {{ workflow_svg | safe }}
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      Drawn deterministically from the repository&rsquo;s own workflow description;
      a build-time check verifies that the drawing matches that description. The
      description is maintained by hand and is not itself generated from the code.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
{% endblock %}
